1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,178
Teacher midterm practice, question 4.

2
00:00:03,798 --> 00:00:08,716
What is the linear atomic density along the one one zero direction in B C C

3
00:00:08,716 --> 00:00:14,552
tungsten, with a lattice constant of zero point three one six five nanometers?

4
00:00:16,252 --> 00:00:19,059
Linear density is the number of atoms centered

5
00:00:19,059 --> 00:00:22,170
on the direction, divided by its length.

6
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:25,953
One one zero is a face diagonal, so its length is root two

7
00:00:25,953 --> 00:00:29,736
times a: zero point four four seven six nanometers.

8
00:00:30,356 --> 00:00:31,987
Which atoms sit on it?

9
00:00:31,987 --> 00:00:37,554
Only the two corner atoms at its ends, each counted as a half, so one atom in total.

10
00:00:37,554 --> 00:00:40,590
The body center atom is not on a face diagonal.

11
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:47,052
Divide: one over zero point four four seven six times ten to the minus nine meters.

12
00:00:47,052 --> 00:00:51,776
That is two point two three four one times ten to the nine per meter.

13
00:00:53,376 --> 00:00:54,461
The answer is A.

14
00:00:55,281 --> 00:00:59,208
In B C C, do not count the center atom on one one zero.

15
00:00:59,208 --> 00:01:04,801
It lies on the body diagonal, one one one, which is the close packed direction.
